[[File:E 407.png|thumb|[[Relic Doge|Relic Doge]], the first example of a Relic enemy]]
'''Relic Enemies''', (古代種 ''Kodaishu'', '''Ancient Species''') are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]] introduced in [[Uncanny Legends]]. Their designs always include the color moss green, typically with runes, veins or orbs that glow with a light green/teal energy. In addition to having extremely high stats overall, most Relics can afflict cats with the [[Curse|curse]] effect, making [[Special Abilities|special abilities]] that target specific types of enemies (i.e. [[Massive Damage|massive damage]], [[Resistant|resistant]], [[Weaken|weaken]]) useless. However, the curse effect doesn't nullify [[Talent Orbs]] or abilities that don't target enemies by trait (e.g., [[Critical Hit]], [[Money Up]], [[Behemoth Slayer]]).

See [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Relic abilities.

*The [[Ototo Corps|Curseblast Foundation]] reduces the damage all [[Cat Units]] take from Relic enemies by 0.75% per level up to a maximum of 15%.
*[[True Form]]s with anti-Relic abilities often require Elder [[Catfruit]], which is obtainable from [[Growing Strange]] after clearing [[Stories of Legend]] (see Growing Strange's article for its schedule). Ironically, Relics themselves do not appear in Growing Strange.
*Relic [[Talent Orbs]] can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Relic|Relic Cradle]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Relic|Relic Summit]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Relic|Relic Frontier]]
**[[Gigahaniwan Strikes!]] [[Continuation Stage]]s: [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!/Cradle Wilderness|Cradle Wilderness]], [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!/Summit Wilderness (Merciless)|Summit Wilderness]], [[Gigahaniwan Strikes!/Frontier Wilderness (Merciless)|Frontier Wilderness]]

==Trivia==
*Relics' "multilayered" designs with a layer of peeling white skin on a green body could possibly be inspired by tree bark, which is supported by the [[Media:Bg228.png|Relic trees]] seen in [[The Face of God/Invasion|The Face of God Invasion]], the roots connected to the [[Origin Base (Enemy Base)|Origin Base]] and the roots that make up [[Sage of Life Dr. Nova]]'s lower body. In this case, the veins seen conducting Relic power through their green innermost layer would represent [[wikipedia:Phloem|phloem]] transporting nutrients to the rest of a tree.
**Many sub-chapters and stages involving trees/forests focus on Relics or introduce new ones, including [[The Endless Wood]], [[Ancient Forest Labyrinth]], [[Eternal Ancient Woods]], [[Sacred Forest]], [[Forest Playground]], [[Tree of Strife]], [[Purple Crystal Forest]] and [[Red Crystal Forest]].
*While the Relic trait's Japanese name, Kodaishu (古代種), translates to "Ancient Species", the kanji 種 can also mean "seed", which may play into Relics' green coloration and tree-like designs.
*[[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Enemy Mecha-Bun]]'s Japanese description directly mentions the Relics before the player first encounters them.
*[[Sir Seal]], [[Teacher Bear]], [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] and [[Kory]] each had multiple Relic variants as Raid Bosses in [[Nyanko Defence Force]].
*Among the masked [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] ([[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]], [[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Masked Yulala]], [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Urs & Fenrir]], [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]], [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Elder Mask Doron]] and [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]]), Ururun is the only one without a Relic enemy counterpart (counting her separately from Urs).
*[[Relic Doge]] and [[Sir Rel]] are the only Relic enemies to appear in the [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]], both in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 3's [[Zombie Outbreaks]].
*Relic Doge and [[Idi:Re]] are the only Relic enemies to appear in [[Stories of Legend]], both in the [[Eldritch Forces/Invasion|Eldritch Forces Invasion]].
*Relic Doge and [[Haniwanwan]] are the only Relic enemies whose Curse abilities aren't guaranteed to activate, while [[Elder Flame Doron]] is the only one who doesn't curse at all.
*Sir Rel and Haniwanwan are the only Relics to have single-target attacks.
*Every stage with Relics has a [[Stage Difficulties|difficulty]] of at least ★8, with the exception of [[Infernal Tower]]'s [[Infernal Tower/Floor 6|Floor 6]].
*Despite being introduced before the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait, Relic came after it in all menus such as the [[Upgrade Menu]] until [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]].
*Relic, Aku and [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] are the only standard enemy types without [[Fruit Treasures]].
*The [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%A4%CE%A4%A4%A4%BA Noise enemies] in [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]] served as both an equivalent and foil to Relic enemies.
**Both specialize in disabling units' trait-specific abilities and are associated with the color green. However, Relics' designs usually include white or gray, while Noise enemies were predominantly black.
**Thematically, the two traits are opposites. Relics are ancient beings with powers from a bygone era, while Noise enemies were futuristic, digital entities such as computer programs or bugs.
**Despite being introduced before [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/t/%A4%A6%A4%A4%A4%EB%A4%B9 Virus enemies], Noise came after Virus in the filter, just as Relic was listed after Aku until Version 13.3.

